; FILED: calling a leaked named-let loop procedure — the remaining divergence is
; on the VM side, and the vm-eskb route differs from vm-src.
;
; The native half of this defect is fixed (a first-class reference to a named-let
; loop procedure now builds a real closure over the shared capture cells instead
; of leaking the bare function pointer, which used to SIGSEGV at the first read
; of a captured variable on both JIT and AOT). What is left is the VM:
;
;   escape through a GLOBAL cell (this file)
;     native -r   2|2|ALIVE
;     native AOT  2|2|ALIVE
;     vm-src      2|2|ALIVE
;     vm-eskb     "2|" then `ERROR: calling non-function at pc=4985 argc=1 type=3`
;
;   escape through a LET-BOUND cell (see below)
;     native -r   2
;     native AOT  2
;     vm-src      `ERROR: calling non-function ... argc=1 type=3`
;     vm-eskb     `ERROR: calling non-function ... argc=1 type=3`
;
; So the compiled-bytecode route loses a loop procedure stored in a global that
; the source route keeps, and neither VM route can call one stored in a let
; binding. Both are the VM's side of the same contract, so this cannot go into
; corpus/ yet: gating it today would fail on the vm-eskb axis for a reason that
; has nothing to do with native.
;
; The native contract is gated meanwhile by
; tests/features/namedlet_escaped_closure_test.esk (15 checks, JIT and AOT).
; Move both shapes below into a corpus entry once the VM can call a leaked loop
; procedure on both routes and through both kinds of escape cell.

; ---- escape through a global cell: vm-src agrees, vm-eskb does not ----
(define g #f)
(define (f)
  (let ((acc 0))
    (let loop ((i 0))
      (if (< i 2) (begin (set! g loop) (set! acc (+ acc 1)) (loop (+ i 1))) acc))))
(display (f))
(display "|")
(display (g 5))
(display "|ALIVE")
(newline)

; ---- escape through a let-bound cell: neither VM route agrees ----
(define (probe)
  (let ((esc #f) (acc 0))
    (let loop ((i 0))
      (if (< i 2) (begin (set! esc loop) (set! acc (+ acc 1)) (loop (+ i 1))) acc))
    (esc 5)))
(display (probe))
(newline)
